    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://atcbosselut.github.io/authors/antoine/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://atcbosselut.github.io/authors/antoine/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I will be joining the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.epfl.ch/schools/ic/&#34;&gt;School of Computer and Communication Sciences&lt;/a&gt; at EPFL as an Assistant Professor in Fall 2021.&lt;/strong&gt; I will be taking on new students when I arrive. Apply this Fall if you are interested in working with me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am a postdoctoral researcher at Stanford University working with &lt;a href=&#34;https://cs.stanford.edu/people/jure/&#34;&gt;Jure Leskovec&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://nlp.stanford.edu/manning/&#34;&gt;Chris Manning&lt;/a&gt;, and the &lt;a href=&#34;https://snap.stanford.edu/&#34;&gt;SNAP&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://nlp.stanford.edu/&#34;&gt;NLP&lt;/a&gt; groups. I completed my PhD at the University of Washington with Professor &lt;a href=&#34;https://homes.cs.washington.edu/~yejin&#34;&gt;Yejin Choi&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My research centers on developing natural language agents that can model, represent, and reason about knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
